window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-73e024a18eb4c45e"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"turn-research-into-a-decision-memo\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">将研究整理成决策备忘录</h1> <p>将证据、取舍和待解决问题汇总到一份建议中。</p> <p>向 ChatGPT 提供研究、规划文档、模型、仪表板、利益相关方背景和未解决问题，然后请它区分证据与解读，并起草一份有来源依据、可供领导层审阅的决策备忘录。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>需要综合内部证据、外部研究、预算和取舍的决策。</li> <li>需要明确证据路径和决策记录的规划或投资问题。</li> <li>希望在领导层审阅前清楚呈现备选方案、负责人确认事项和未解决风险的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>读取已批准的回顾记录、规划文档、模型和源材料。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/notion\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">notion（需联网）</a></td> <td>如果决策历史、研究笔记和项目背景位于 Notion，则检查相关内容。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack（需联网）</a></td> <td>查看已批准频道或讨论串中的利益相关方讨论、评论和待解决问题。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>核验建议背后的财务、KPI 或情景输入。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>制作简明、可编辑的决策备忘录和供会前审阅的材料，并注明来源。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>起草决策备忘录</p> <p>建议模型：<code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> · 建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">我正在决定是否应该由 [team or company] 执行 [decision]。\n\n请使用以下来源：\n- 往期回顾和研究：[files or links]\n- 规划文档、模型和仪表板：[files or links]\n- 受众、账户或市场背景：[files or links]\n- 利益相关方评论和会议笔记：[files, channels, or thread links]\n- 预算边界：[files or links]\n- 决策标准：[criteria]\n\n如果我要求进行网络研究，请将外部发现与内部证据分开。撰写一份简明的决策备忘录，包含建议、支持证据、备选方案和取舍、成本、风险、决策记录、待解决问题、负责人确认事项及来源链接。\n\n如果受众需要会前阅读材料，请将备忘录及支持分析整理成便于审阅的资料包，同时以备忘录作为事实依据。标出假设，不要替我作出决定，也不要分享输出。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/how-to-use-codex-for-everyday-work/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy：日常工作（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/codex-for-work/how-business-operations-teams-use-codex/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy：业务运营团队（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"define-the-decision-before-gathering-evidence\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">收集证据前先明确决策</h2> <p>如果 ChatGPT 清楚要作出的选择、约束条件、受众、决策日期和审批边界，决策工作就会更清晰。先附上内部背景资料，然后单独指出需要完成的外部研究。</p> <ol> <li>说明要作出的决策、决策者、时间安排和判断标准。</li> <li>附上回顾记录、规划文档、模型、仪表板、预算边界、利益相关方评论和会议笔记。</li> <li>请 ChatGPT 列出内部证据、来源缺口、尚未解决的分歧和需要进行的网络研究。</li> <li>运行起始提示词，并审查建议、备选方案、取舍、风险、决策记录和缺失信息。</li> <li>在备忘录进入领导层审阅前，核实每项重要主张和负责人确认事项。</li> </ol> <p>请将内部证据、外部研究和解读分开。如果某项成本、日期或市场事实无法核实，就将它保留为明确的待解决事项。当受众需要更长的会前阅读材料时，应以决策备忘录作为事实依据，并将支持性分析放在附录中，而不是把不确定性隐藏在润色后的幻灯片里。</p> <p><a id=\"pressure-test-the-recommendation-and-review-packet\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">压力测试建议和审阅材料</h2> <p>使用后续提示词挑战当前首选方案，找出哪些假设变化会改变建议，并预判决策者可能提出的问题。</p> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Pressure-test the decision memo.\n\nShow:\n\n- the assumptions that drive the recommendation\n- the strongest case for each alternative\n- evidence that is internal versus external\n- costs, risks, and missing information that could change the decision\n- claims, numbers, and owner confirmations that still need review\n- questions a skeptical decision maker is likely to ask\n- the smallest additional analysis needed to reduce uncertainty\n\nKeep the original memo unchanged, cite the relevant source for each finding, and mark every proposed revision for review.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请对这份决策备忘录进行压力检验。\n\n说明：\n\n- 哪些假设决定了建议\n- 每个备选方案最有力的支持理由\n- 哪些证据来自内部，哪些来自外部\n- 哪些成本、风险和缺失信息可能改变决策\n- 哪些主张、数字和负责人确认仍需审阅\n- 持怀疑态度的决策者可能提出哪些问题\n- 为降低不确定性，还需要开展哪些最少量的补充分析\n\n保持原备忘录不变，为每项发现引用相关来源，并将每项建议修改都标为待审阅。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"turn-research-into-a-decision-memo\">Turn research into a decision memo</h1> <p>Combine evidence, tradeoffs, and open questions into one recommendation.</p> <p>Give ChatGPT research, planning documents, models, dashboards, stakeholder context, and unresolved questions, then ask it to separate evidence from interpretation and draft a sourced decision memo that is ready for leadership review.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Decisions that combine internal evidence, external research, budget, and tradeoffs.</li> <li>Planning or investment questions where the recommendation needs an explicit evidence trail and decision log.</li> <li>Teams that want alternatives, owner confirmations, and unresolved risks visible before a leadership review.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read approved recaps, planning docs, models, and source material.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/notion\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">notion (online)</a></td> <td>Check decision history, research notes, and project context when they live in Notion.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">slack (online)</a></td> <td>Review stakeholder debate, comments, and unresolved questions from approved channels or threads.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$spreadsheets</code></td> <td>Validate financial, KPI, or scenario inputs behind the recommendation.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>Produce a concise, editable decision memo and review-ready pre-read with source notes.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Draft a decision memo</p> <p>Suggested model：<code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> · Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">I'm deciding whether [team or company] should [decision].\n\nUse these sources:\n- prior recaps and research: [files or links]\n- planning docs, models, and dashboards: [files or links]\n- audience, account, or market context: [files or links]\n- stakeholder comments and meeting notes: [files, channels, or thread links]\n- budget guardrails: [files or links]\n- decision criteria: [criteria]\n\nIf I ask for web research, keep external findings separate from internal evidence. Write a concise decision memo with a recommendation, supporting evidence, alternatives and tradeoffs, costs, risks, a decision log, open questions, owner confirmations, and source links.\n\nIf the audience needs a pre-read, organize the memo and supporting analysis into a review-ready packet while keeping the memo as the source of truth. Flag assumptions and do not make the decision or share the output.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/how-to-use-codex-for-everyday-work/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy: Everyday work (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://openai.com/academy/codex-for-work/how-business-operations-teams-use-codex/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">OpenAI Academy: Business operations teams (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"define-the-decision-before-gathering-evidence\">Define the decision before gathering evidence</h2> <p>Decision work becomes clearer when ChatGPT knows the choice, constraints, audience, decision date, and approval boundary. Attach internal context first, then identify any outside research that needs to be completed separately.</p> <ol> <li>State the decision, decision maker, timing, and criteria.</li> <li>Attach recaps, planning docs, models, dashboards, budget guardrails, stakeholder comments, and meeting notes.</li> <li>Ask ChatGPT to inventory internal evidence, source gaps, unresolved debate, and requested web research.</li> <li>Run the starter prompt and review the recommendation, alternatives, tradeoffs, risks, decision log, and missing information.</li> <li>Verify each material claim and owner confirmation before the memo enters leadership review.</li> </ol> <p>Keep internal evidence, external research, and interpretation in separate sections. If a cost, date, or market fact cannot be confirmed, leave it as an explicit open item. When the audience needs a longer pre-read, keep the decision memo as the source of truth and place supporting analysis in an appendix instead of hiding uncertainty in polished slides.</p> <h2 id=\"pressure-test-the-recommendation-and-review-packet\">Pressure-test the recommendation and review packet</h2> <p>Use a follow-up pass to challenge the preferred option, expose which assumptions would change the recommendation, and anticipate the questions decision makers will ask.</p> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Pressure-test the decision memo.\n\nShow:\n\n- the assumptions that drive the recommendation\n- the strongest case for each alternative\n- evidence that is internal versus external\n- costs, risks, and missing information that could change the decision\n- claims, numbers, and owner confirmations that still need review\n- questions a skeptical decision maker is likely to ask\n- the smallest additional analysis needed to reduce uncertainty\n\nKeep the original memo unchanged, cite the relevant source for each finding, and mark every proposed revision for review.\n</code></pre>"};
